'''Buna''' is a [[Torricelli languages|Torricelli language]] of [[Marienberg Rural LLG]], [[East Sepik Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]].

There are two divergent dialects. One dialect is spoken in Kasmin ({{coord|-4.018975|144.060235|type:city_region:PG|name=Kasmin 1}}), Boig ({{coord|-3.84861|144.054923|type:city_region:PG|name=Boik}}), Waskurin ({{coord|-3.870089|144.068112|type:city_region:PG|name=Waskurin}}), and Arapang ({{coord|-3.88039|144.073217|type:city_region:PG|name=Ariapan}}) villages, and another in Masan, Mangan ({{coord|-3.953676|144.239463|type:city_region:PG|name=Mangan}}), and Garien villages.<ref name=e25/><ref name="UN-PNG">{{cite web |url=https://data.humdata.org/dataset/village-coordinates-lookup |title=Papua New Guinea Village Coordinates Lookup |author=United Nations in Papua New Guinea |work=Humanitarian Data Exchange |version=1.31.9 |date=2018}}</ref>

